    <h1>Facing Criminal or Immigration Proceedings in the Philippines?</h1>
    <p class="service-lede">Coordinated support when criminal and immigration matters intersect.</p>

    <p>Foreign nationals involved in criminal or other legal proceedings can also face immigration consequences involving their visa, immigration record, detention, deportation or ability to remain in the Philippines. FIS brings the immigration and legal sides of the matter together through one coordinated service. Our coordinated service includes access to qualified Philippine legal counsel where legal representation is required, while FIS manages the connected immigration work and coordinates the matter as a whole.</p>

    <div id="urgent-assistance" class="service-cta service-cta--top">
      <p class="service-cta__actions">
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/contact/?service=legal-support">Make an Enquiry</a>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/?service=legal-support&amp;priority=urgent">Request Urgent Assistance</a>
      </p>
      <p class="muted">Use urgent assistance for time-sensitive matters such as arrest or detention, imminent immigration action, urgent criminal or immigration proceedings, or another matter requiring prompt attention. For a general legal-support enquiry that is not time-sensitive, use Make an Enquiry instead.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="proposition-highlight">
      <h2>One Coordinated Team When Immigration and Legal Matters Intersect</h2>
      <p>When a legal matter also creates immigration consequences, handling each side separately can create gaps in timing, documentation and case coordination. FIS brings the relevant workstreams together through one coordinated service, managing the immigration component while providing access to qualified Philippine legal counsel where legal representation is required. This means you are not left coordinating separate providers while dealing with an already serious situation.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>How We Can Assist</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Assessing the immigration consequences arising from the connected legal matter</li>
      <li>Reviewing the relevant immigration records, notices, orders or proceedings</li>
      <li>Identifying the immigration response that needs to run alongside the legal matter</li>
      <li>Preparing and organising the supporting immigration documentation</li>
      <li>Coordinating documentation and developments across the immigration and legal workstreams</li>
      <li>Providing access to qualified Philippine legal counsel through the coordinated service where legal representation is required</li>
      <li>Liaising with the Bureau of Immigration and managing the immigration-facing process</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Why Coordinated Support Matters</h2>
    <p>A criminal or other legal proceeding and an immigration matter can involve different processes while affecting the same foreign national, and developments in one can be relevant to the other. Handling them through disconnected providers can leave you responsible for relaying information, coordinating documents and keeping each side updated on what the other is doing. FIS coordinates the immigration and legal workstreams so the relevant parts of your matter are managed together.</p>

    <h2>Common Situations We Handle</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Criminal proceedings with connected immigration consequences</li>
      <li>Detention or deportation-related immigration matters</li>
      <li>Immigration proceedings arising alongside an ongoing legal matter</li>
      <li>Matters requiring both immigration case management and Philippine legal representation</li>
      <li>Urgent matters requiring coordinated immigration and legal action</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How the Process Works</h2>
    <ol class="step-list">
      <li>
        <h3>Tell Us What Is Happening</h3>
        <p>Tell us about the matter and share the records, notices or documents available to you.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Coordinated Assessment</h3>
        <p>FIS assesses the immigration implications and identifies the immigration and legal workstreams that need to be addressed.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Immigration &amp; Legal Case Management</h3>
        <p>FIS manages the immigration component. Where legal representation is required, the coordinated service includes access to qualified Philippine legal counsel for the connected legal work.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Follow-Through</h3>
        <p>FIS follows up on the immigration process, coordinates developments between the workstreams, and keeps you informed. You can track the progress of your transaction through the FIS Client Portal.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>

